       - fg touches all 4 edges (top row, bottom row, left col, right col each have >=1 fg)
       - fg pixel count is roughly 40-70% of h*w (reject or resample if outside)
    4. Place the bbox at a random position inside the 9x9 grid (with >=1 margin)
    5. Output = np.repeat(np.repeat(crop, 2, axis=0), 2, axis=1)
